{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"3275","artifact_type":"feature-context","name":"plan/feature-context-provider-neutral-cache-bypass.md@sha256:a4918db1a8d1278f0a7e51fee6ae84bea3059141e6052f75cb19b4bb1dc3d23a"},"owner_reference":"3275","content":"# ARTIFACT:DISCOVERY\n\n## Feature\n\nProvider-neutral cache-bypass option for backlog_list and backlog_view\n\n## Problem Statement\n\nThe backlog MCP/CLI tools are meant to be provider-neutral (the configured backend can be GitHub,\nBeads, SQLite, or Memory; `SyncProvider` protocol at `backlog_core/backend_types.py:203` gates\ncache/reconciliation behavior backend-agnostically throughout `operations.py`). Despite that,\n`backlog_list`'s cache-refresh parameter is named `from_github` (`backlog_core/server.py:1936`),\nnaming one specific backend on a tool meant to work across all of them \u2014 inconsistent even with\nits own sibling reconcile/pull tool, which already uses the provider-neutral name `full_refresh`\n(`server.py:1624`). Separately, `backlog_view` has no bypass-cache option at all across its full\nparameter set \u2014 it always reads local cache with no way to check the live backend first.\n\nThis caused a real problem in session: while verifying whether recently-groomed content\n(items #3169/#3268) had actually reached GitHub, `backlog_view` could not answer the question \u2014\nit shows correctly-synced-looking content regardless of whether anything reached the remote\nbackend, because it never consults the backend directly. Confirming required shelling out to\n`gh issue view` directly, which itself took multiple attempts because it wasn't obvious which\nGitHub field corresponds to this system's authoritative record.\n\n## Goals\n\n1. Every backlog command that reads cached data gets a consistent, provider-neutral way to bypass\n   that cache and validate against the raw backend.\n2. `backlog_view` gains a live-backend-check capability, matching what `backlog_list` already\n   offers via `from_github`.\n3. The cache-refresh parameter name on `backlog_list` no longer names a specific backend.\n4. A live check must resolve content through the same resolution path the existing reconciliation\n   logic already uses \u2014 for GitHub specifically, through the append-only audit-comment record via\n   its head pointer (`backlog_core/ARCHITECTURE.md:780-789`), never by reading the visible issue\n   body as if it were authoritative.\n\n## Anti-Goals\n\n1. Not building a new cache invalidation/expiry system \u2014 scoped to an explicit per-call bypass.\n2. Not redesigning the existing reconciliation/resolution logic \u2014 reuse it as-is.\n3. Not altering what data is considered authoritative per backend \u2014 that's already decided\n   (audit-comment record for GitHub, per ARCHITECTURE.md).\n\n## Requirements\n\n### Functional\n\n1. `backlog_list` exposes its cache-refresh capability under a name that does not reference any\n   specific backend.\n2. `backlog_view` exposes an equivalent bypass-cache/live-check parameter, currently absent from\n   its full parameter set (`selector`, `head`, `include_content`, `limit`, `map`, `navigate`,\n   `offset`, `section`, `sections`, `show`, `since`, `skip_tokens`, `summary`).\n3. When the live-check path is used against GitHub, content is resolved via the existing\n   audit-comment/head-pointer logic, not the raw issue body field.\n4. Both CLI and MCP surfaces for affected commands expose consistent parameter naming/behavior.\n\n### Non-Functional\n\n1. Naming consistency: the chosen parameter name is shared across every backlog command that\n   gains this capability, and matches (or aligns with) the sibling tool's existing `full_refresh`.\n2. No backend-naive raw-storage reads \u2014 every live-check path goes through the same\n   backend-appropriate resolution logic the reconciliation code already uses.\n\n## Design Questions for Planning\n\n1. User's item text states the fix \"must not read a backend's raw storage naively... has to go\n   through the same resolution path the existing reconciliation logic already uses\" \u2014 this is a\n   correctness constraint on the mechanism, not a specific proposed API; planning should confirm\n   which existing reconciliation code path is reused (`operations.py` sync/reconcile logic\n   referenced at lines 1168, 1596, 3079, 3739, 3816, 3875, 3925) rather than building a new one.\n2. What exact provider-neutral name should replace `from_github` on `backlog_list`, and what name\n   should `backlog_view` use \u2014 reuse the sibling tool's existing `full_refresh` name for\n   consistency, or introduce a new shared name used by all three (list/view/pull)?\n3. Should `from_github` be renamed outright (breaking change to the MCP tool signature) or kept\n   as a deprecated alias for backward compatibility? No existing callers were found in this repo\n   at discovery time (see Resolved Questions), which weakly favors an outright rename, but\n   external MCP clients are out of view.\n4. The item says \"every backlog command that reads cached data\" should get this \u2014 planning needs\n   to enumerate which commands besides `backlog_list`/`backlog_view` actually read a local cache\n   (candidates from `operations.py`: any read-path gated by the `SyncProvider` checkpoint/cache\n   logic near lines 1168, 1596, 3079, 3739, 3816, 3875, 3925) versus which only mutate.\n\n## References\n\n- `backlog_core/server.py:1936` \u2014 `backlog_list`'s `from_github` parameter\n- `backlog_core/server.py:1624` \u2014 sibling `full_refresh` parameter (provider-neutral precedent)\n- `backlog_core/backend_types.py:203` \u2014 `SyncProvider` protocol\n- `backlog_core/operations.py:1168,1596,3079,3739,3816,3875,3925` \u2014 cache/reconciliation gating\n- `backlog_core/ARCHITECTURE.md:780-789` \u2014 GitHub authoritative-record resolution (audit-comment\n  record via head pointer, issue body never authoritative)\n- Backlog item #3275; session context items #3169, #3268 (grooming-reached-GitHub verification)\n\n## Resolved Questions\n\n| Question | Answer | Source |\n|----------|--------|--------|\n| Any prior implementation of this rename/feature already exists? | No \u2014 `git log`/`merged-prs` search for `from_github` and related terms found no commit or merged PR implementing this rename or a `backlog_view` bypass-cache option; `server.py:1936`/`1624` still show the described state as of grooming time. | git log, backlog merged-prs, direct source read (2026-08-29) |\n\n## Open Questions\n\n- None blocking. All open items are design decisions routed to Design Questions for Planning\n  above (auto mode \u2014 no human interaction performed; see [AUTO] log in session).\n\n## User Confirmation\n\n- [x] Auto mode: treated as confirmed per discovery skill's AutoMode gate (no design questions\n  are unbound constraints, domain-knowledge gaps, or contradictory requirements).\n"}